One small decision the plan didn't specify: since a single interval whose end > start is valid, and sorting equal starts by end for determinism, I used `a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1]` as the comparator. Validation happens during the copy pass, so an invalid (out-of-order) input still throws a `RangeError` before any merge logic runs.
